Chapter 4: My Job.

That moment, staring my sister's case worker in the eye, putting my self, my family, at risk of angering the demigods that had ruined by life, because my sister needed me. That is when I started my job, the job I still have. To advocate for my people. Its not my sister that needs saving now. (She's incredibly happy and 'successful' by my reckoning. Very happy with Uncle, who she now refers to as her "ex husband" and is legally her wife. She is being a great parent to he 4 children they had together, and the 5 more children she fathered on Uncle's younger sisters, and is well on her way to founding her own clan like mother always wanted.)

But that doesn't mean I can stop. As modern medicine and pre-modern breeding patters collide, more and more catgirls leave our home timeline to try and find food and shelter in the Pan-Sentient-Community, (all too often just humans putting a "All species welcome sticker" on the door of a cafeteria that doesn't serve any non-vegan dairy.), and so new 'problems', new misunderstandings, new completely avoidable tragedies are happening every day.

Of course back then, back at the moment, would I have made the same choice if I knew just how hard it would be? Yes, actually, I think so. Maybe its vanity on my part but I do think I would have choose to give up being exactly the woman my mother expected of me, to face the challenges I do every day, to be, by my grandmother's standards a failure: I have only a single granddaughter and will likely never have more. I have had years where nothing I did seemed to make anything better, and it felt like the whole world hated me for daring to care about people, but.. I don't for a moment regret the choices I made, starting at that moment. I don't regret doing the right thing. If there's one thing I want you to take from this book, its not "Catgirls life cycles are fundamentally different then primate sapients", its not even "Maybe in a situation where you have no real idea what is going on, you shouldn't default to the most extrema action possible", it's "Its okay to do the right thing, even when it hurts".

The only one of the three things I demanded that my sister get that is actually _needed_ for our pregnancies is the butter. If you don't give us some proof that there is someone who our babies can nurse, then we _will_ miscarry. Its just not worth the risk. Butter is basically a way to trick our bodies into thinking there's more milk available then they are eating,, a super stimulus if you will, unaged cheese, or just a glass of whole milk every day will also work. As for the cow-heart, that's just that we A) always need more meat then you do, and B) think its the best "cut" of beef.

Despite what some of our healers will say, we don't _need_ to drink semen, and despite what others of our healers will say, no, we can't get any significant amount of nutrition though our vaginas. But when your unborn baby is trying to drain your life force through its belly button, or when just smelling your mother's tea or roofing tar from three blocks away, is enough to make you vomit so much you feel like you might have given birth though your nose, being able to crawl into your husbsands arms and have her prove she still loves you and your body even as it punishes you is.. is very nice. It helps. It helps a lot.

You might think that not being able to taste sweet would mean we wouldn't like fruit, and well many of the nonsentient members of our clade, who specialized in meat just a bit more, don't. It is true that our diets have a lot more nuts/oils/creamy plant products then the clasical starchy sweet fruit like an sweet apple or mild lemon, but we also actually have more abilities to pick up on flavors then you do, and a just as strong prefrence for .. just weird tasting things. We love hot pepers like you do. Those of use who can eat chocolate and not throw up, or get the runs, love it (the lucky bastards). Tea, coffee, bayleaves, mint, pretty much all your spices, we love them. We can even grow to like the alergic reaction celery gives us. My mothers cooking was doused in mint for example. We are biological carnivours like wolves, we really cant go vegan for more then about 6 months and pushing that in our bearing years can actually in perminant sterility. (Mostly though we will just get constipaited and sleepy and kind of ... dumb.) but like racoons or bears, we crave varity and a wide range of food.

The situation that let to my mother emmegrating is saddly common among poeple who humanity is trying to help. Humans come in and give us vaccines and medicines and nutritional gummies, and so every single family in the whole area decides that clearly right now is a boom time, and the thing to do is have as many daughters as possible to help farm or work or trade. And then those daughters grow up and decide the same thing. And then those daughters and grand daughters grow up, and suddenly there's not land nor opprotunity for later daughters or traveling 'sons',

When my mother was growing up they delt with this in the traditional way. Give only enough food to the youngest girls to keep them alive, deliberately give them just meat, no dairy, not much fat, very little nuts and fruit. This keeps them alive, but also stops their ovulation, and causes any that are pregnant to miscarry.

And so, when my mother came to Canada, and found that her job let her afford basically as much exotic fruit and milk-fats as she could possibly want, she fell in love with a dozen different ones, and her, and mine, and my sister's, favorite is pineapple.